  "body": "### Summary\nAs a reader, I want a landing on a post (or a scroll restore) never to be undone by WebKit's late reset of a new document, so that the reader opens where I asked.\n\n### Evidence (inference, not yet observed in the app)\n- CI job 138855383148 (#1324, analysed in PR #1330): `pageAway()` had seen both the page and the scroll view at 300, and the page was back at the top within five animation frames. That is WebKit's late reset of a new document (#995), arriving after the point where the app considers the page settled.\n- In the app, a restore made at that moment would be undone. Only `WebKitResetWatch`'s second chance (`WebKitResetWatch.swift:47-50`) may cover it.\n- Seen on the CI runtime (iOS 27.0), never in 28 local runs on iOS 27.2.\n\n### Scope\n- Check whether a real landing or restore can be undone by a late reset after `pageAway()`. Use a hosted reader on iOS 27.0 if available, or log the reset timing on CI.\n- If it can, make the landing wait for the reset in the app (the reader's agreement step, `reader.js:293-306`), not only in tests.\n- Never guess: measure first.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] A test or measurement shows whether the app path is exposed.\n- [ ] If it is, a fix with a test that fails without it.\n\nFrom the adversarial review of #1330 (Fable 5.2, r1330), finding 1.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
